# Third-party downloaded VASP outputs (nal-hfo archive, 189 MB, 152 files).
# Not ours to redistribute; POTCAR was already excluded at extraction time.
# The scientific/workflow audit of this archive IS tracked, at
# reports/external_vasp_archive_audit_20260824/README.md
external_data/

# pytest temporary directories (distinct from .pytest_cache/)
.pytest_tmp_*/

# Licensed VASP pseudopotentials. Never commit or redistribute.
# The nal-hfo extraction already excluded all seven POTCAR members; the
# generated strain-pilot job dirs carry POTCAR_NOT_INCLUDED.txt placeholders,
# which ARE meant to be tracked - they document the deliberate omission.
POTCAR
POTCAR.*
POTCAR_*
!POTCAR_NOT_INCLUDED.txt

# Downloaded literature/data archives. The nal-hfo source .tgz lives outside
# this repo (D:\Code-X\Ferroelectric knowledgegraph\), so this is defensive.
*.tgz
*.tar.gz
# ... except the hash-frozen TEFS upload bundle. Its SHA-256 is recorded in
# reports/phase_strain_computation_preflight_20260824/REMOTE_EXECUTION_GATE.md
# and gates a paid submission, so the artefact must travel with its hash.
!computations/phase_strain_pilot/tefs_single_job_pilot_v0_1/output/*.tar.gz

# Report artefacts that embed verbatim excerpts from copyrighted papers
# (phase_evidence_text / evidence_a / evidence_b / machine_supporting_quote /
# direct_phase_evidence, up to ~800 chars each, thousands of rows, mostly
# paywalled DOIs). README already bars "解析文本" from the GitHub repo.
# These are regenerable locally, read-only, with no LLM cost:
#   python pipelines/64_run_phase_competition_workflow.py \
#     --db-path <db> --output-dir reports/<new_run>
# Their summary/*.json siblings carry only counts, hashes and paths and ARE
# tracked - keep it that way.
reports/**/phase_observation_annotation_queue.csv
reports/**/phase_contradiction_candidates.csv
reports/**/phase_contradiction_candidates.jsonl
reports/**/paper_group_inventory.csv
reports/**/phase_machine_preannotations.csv
reports/**/phase_machine_preannotations.jsonl
